hrough.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Tom McClintock (R) is running."]}, "overview": "California's 5th District, spanning the Sierra foothills and parts of the Central Valley, leans Republican by about ten points, and incumbent Tom McClintock is seeking another term. He holds a clear financial edge, raising roughly $929,000 to Democrat Michael Masuda's $362,000, along with a larger cash reserve. Masuda has campaigned on small Central Valley towns and drawn local press attention and an editorial endorsement, but no outside groups have spent on his behalf.\n\nEvery major race rater places the seat in the Safe or Solid Republican column, with one calling it Likely Republican, and prediction markets give Masuda roughly a 9% chance. No public general-election polls exist, keeping uncertainty wider than usual. The evidence points to a double-digit McClintock win, with an upset possible only if a strong Democratic environment reaches this district in force.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1154, "margin": -9.09}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1311, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0595, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0545, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0432, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0323, "margin": -12.8}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.033, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0389, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0405, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0135, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0503, "margin": -12.0}]}